WEBVTT

00:00:40.650 --> 00:00:44.280
This procedure will decide the fate of Germany,

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:46.920
as well as the rest of world.

00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:51.330
Theoretically, the current 
success rate is about 20%.

00:00:52.230 --> 00:00:56.520
If this is a success, we'll be able 
to use organisms other than insects.

00:00:57.930 --> 00:01:01.140
But must we use a child?

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:05.460
We have custody over their children.

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:10.190
If we use children we'll be able 
to observe them long-term, as well.

00:01:10.190 --> 00:01:12.880
Are you saying we're going 
to take their entire lives away?

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:31.130
Now, then... How about you?

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:43.090
We'd prefer not to have to
 force one of you, if possible.

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:51.960
I...

00:01:56.330 --> 00:01:58.270
I'll do it.

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:07.640
I see that you care for your friends.

00:02:08.050 --> 00:02:10.030
S1042,

00:02:10.630 --> 00:02:12.160
what is your name?

00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:18.300
Adolf... Reinhardt.

00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:25.630
We will now begin the Mosaic Organ operation

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:29.670
on subject code number 
S1042, Adolf Reinhardt.

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:14.010
<b><i>Electric Organism</i></b>

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:37.250
She never ceases to amaze me. 
Isabella is amazing.

00:04:37.250 --> 00:04:39.880
I sort of feel bad for letting 
her do this all by herself.

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:41.700
We don't have a choice.

00:04:41.700 --> 00:04:44.590
If we went out there, 
we'd be killed in an instant.

00:04:44.590 --> 00:04:46.010
We're pathetic.

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:50.260
<i>You should head to the 
crash site of the Annex 1.</i>

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:54.870
<i>This is urgent, Adolf. 
Get there before China or Russia.</i>

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:56.900
Understood.

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:58.120
<i>I'm counting on you.</i>

00:04:58.120 --> 00:05:03.550
I wonder why they used such useless 
creatures for our operations.

00:05:03.550 --> 00:05:04.750
It would have been nice

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:07.760
to at least get powers
 we could actually fight with.

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:10.240
You'll all have to fight regardless.

00:05:10.460 --> 00:05:13.620
As soon as you step outside, 
whether you like it or not...

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:17.880
If you have time to complain 
about your powers,

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:20.820
think about how to make them useful.

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:29.060
No one is useless in this division.

00:05:29.700 --> 00:05:32.970
Tell Isabella to wrap it up. 
We're departing immediately.

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:34.270
Y-Yes, sir.

00:06:04.090 --> 00:06:07.270
<i>He dodged before anything 
even showed up on the radar...</i>

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:09.510
<i>This is the division leader's power?</i>

00:06:09.910 --> 00:06:12.760
We're going to prepare to takeoff. 
Brace for acceleration.

00:06:12.760 --> 00:06:13.820
Why?

00:07:12.860 --> 00:07:15.600
<i>No. 4 Division's escape vessel...</i>

00:07:15.600 --> 00:07:18.020
<i>Apparently they didn't</i>

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:21.190
<i>betray us.</i>

00:07:23.700 --> 00:07:24.630
Isabella.

00:07:28.960 --> 00:07:31.330
Just wait here like a good little girl.

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:46.130
Now, then. There's only 
one thing to do, Isabella.

00:07:46.620 --> 00:07:49.030
Steal No. 4 Division's escape vessel

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:52.030
from that reckless driving fatso.

00:07:52.600 --> 00:07:53.530
Gotcha.

00:07:56.990 --> 00:08:02.290
I'll take care of the 300 
or so that are over there.

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:25.560
You know... you really shouldn't 
gang up on people like that.

00:08:33.910 --> 00:08:35.780
Humans...

00:08:36.680 --> 00:08:38.180
are pretty weak.

00:09:05.060 --> 00:09:06.180
<i>Electricity.</i>

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:08.090
<i>There is an organism that is</i>

00:09:08.090 --> 00:09:10.300
<i>born with the ability to control 
this scientific phenomenon.</i>

00:09:11.410 --> 00:09:12.780
<i>The electric eel.</i>

00:09:13.430 --> 00:09:15.090
<i>It is an apex predator that stands</i>

00:09:15.090 --> 00:09:17.570
<i>at the top of the food chain 
in the South American Amazon.</i>

00:09:17.570 --> 00:09:19.200
<i>It is called an eel,</i>

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:22.470
<i>but it is a species that has evolved 
in a completely different way.</i>

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:24.920
<i>Its ability to discharge electricity</i>

00:09:24.920 --> 00:09:28.380
<i>has been perfected to wound
or kill its prey and enemies.</i>

00:09:28.380 --> 00:09:31.890
<i>It is the only species in its genus.</i>

00:09:34.520 --> 00:09:38.090
Six terraformar samples captured.

00:09:38.360 --> 00:09:41.100
No wonder he told us not to get out.

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:43.860
Not only would we be in the way out there,

00:09:43.860 --> 00:09:45.940
we would have been caught 
up in that, as well.

00:09:45.940 --> 00:09:47.850
Yeah, seriously...

00:09:49.830 --> 00:09:52.480
Hey, pay attention.

00:09:54.690 --> 00:09:57.110
It's too bad about your muscles.

00:09:57.770 --> 00:10:01.120
If you weren't a roachy bastard, 
you'd totally be my type.

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:05.550
<i>When the electric eel emits electricity,</i>

00:10:05.550 --> 00:10:07.560
<i>it also receives an electric shock.</i>

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:11.700
<i>However, the thick fat in 
its body acts as insulation,</i>

00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:14.120
<i>and it is able to escape fatal wounds.</i>

00:10:19.610 --> 00:10:23.250
<i>That goes the same for Adolf, 
who has grounding devices</i>

00:10:23.250 --> 00:10:24.970
<i>implanted throughout his body.</i>

00:10:36.450 --> 00:10:37.990
It's a success.

00:10:38.860 --> 00:10:42.000
But at this rate, 
the subject's body won't hold.

00:10:50.260 --> 00:10:52.250
<i>Well done, Adolf-kun.</i>

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:55.000
<i>It appears your control 
is getting better.</i>

00:10:55.900 --> 00:10:58.710
<i>We should reevaluate the grounding devices.</i>

00:10:59.190 --> 00:11:01.420
<i>Let's end things for today.</i>

00:11:13.530 --> 00:11:16.310
<i>My life was already bought by someone else.</i>

00:11:18.190 --> 00:11:20.890
<i>I had no other choice</i>

00:11:21.530 --> 00:11:26.540
<i>but to continue working for the army 
and helping with their experiments.</i>

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:33.380
<i>I kept thinking over and over how I would</i>

00:11:35.430 --> 00:11:37.420
<i>escape their monitoring and die.</i>

00:11:43.380 --> 00:11:45.280
<i>Until I met her...</i>

00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:32.000
You're Adolf Reinhardt-kun, right?

00:12:35.890 --> 00:12:37.940
You're in my Spanish class, aren't you?

00:12:38.450 --> 00:12:42.010
I'm Rosa Zypries. Don't you remember me?

00:12:43.570 --> 00:12:45.450
No, sorry.

00:12:47.850 --> 00:12:49.380
Fine, then.

00:12:49.380 --> 00:12:51.660
This will just have to 
be our first meeting.

00:13:04.280 --> 00:13:06.130
Is it okay for me to sit here?

00:13:06.130 --> 00:13:07.150
Yeah...

00:13:07.630 --> 00:13:08.640
That's fine.

00:13:09.780 --> 00:13:13.640
<i>It was on that day that my life changed.</i>

00:13:21.120 --> 00:13:22.410
Good morning!

00:13:22.780 --> 00:13:24.000
Come on, now.

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:26.070
You shouldn't be slouching 
first thing in the morning.

00:13:27.120 --> 00:13:28.730
R-Right...

00:13:29.290 --> 00:13:30.240
You think so?

00:13:33.860 --> 00:13:36.360
Yeah, you look much better like that.

00:13:36.360 --> 00:13:37.690
All right, I'll see you later.

00:13:37.690 --> 00:13:39.080
H-Hey!

00:13:39.080 --> 00:13:40.560
Wait, Rosa!

00:13:41.860 --> 00:13:43.010
Do you know him?

00:13:43.330 --> 00:13:45.680
We just became friends the other day.

00:13:45.680 --> 00:13:48.010
I thought he was sort of scary.

00:13:48.010 --> 00:13:51.390
Not at all! He was even feeding the pigeons.

00:13:54.900 --> 00:13:59.390
Huh... So your birthday's 
December 25th, Ado-kun?

00:13:59.840 --> 00:14:00.770
Yeah...

00:14:01.090 --> 00:14:04.680
So that means you only get one 
present for both Christmas and your

00:14:04.680 --> 00:14:06.530
birthday from your parents, huh?

00:14:06.530 --> 00:14:09.420
Oh, yeah. I totally had a friend like that.

00:14:09.420 --> 00:14:13.660
Then why don't you two 
go on a date that day?

00:14:13.930 --> 00:14:16.910
Huh?! Wh-Where did that come from?!

00:14:17.140 --> 00:14:19.670
You said you were free on Christmas.

00:14:20.230 --> 00:14:21.540
Are you free, Adolf-kun?

00:14:21.540 --> 00:14:22.390
Huh?

00:14:23.230 --> 00:14:23.940
Well, yeah...

00:14:23.940 --> 00:14:25.340
All right, it's settled, then.

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:26.000
Huh?

00:14:26.000 --> 00:14:26.800
Wha?

00:14:26.800 --> 00:14:28.320
Seriously?

00:14:28.320 --> 00:14:29.590
Great job, Adolf!

00:14:29.590 --> 00:14:31.470
What about me?

00:14:31.470 --> 00:14:32.690
You idiot!

00:14:38.950 --> 00:14:39.850
Here?

00:14:40.380 --> 00:14:44.500
Yeah. Apparently the night view from 
the bridge nearby is really pretty.

00:14:44.830 --> 00:14:47.730
Apparently this is a good place to 
spend some time until evening.

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:55.450
Maybe...

00:14:56.780 --> 00:14:58.460
This is sort of meh.

00:15:01.620 --> 00:15:03.730
I'm having fun.

00:15:03.730 --> 00:15:04.750
Really?

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:08.060
Apparently electric eels make 
the Christmas tree light up.

00:15:08.060 --> 00:15:09.490
I wanna see!

00:15:09.490 --> 00:15:10.630
Hey, can we wait and see?

00:15:11.550 --> 00:15:14.370
Your papa is waiting outside, 
so we can't take too long.

00:15:14.370 --> 00:15:15.220
Okay.

00:15:15.660 --> 00:15:17.470
I wonder how it makes electricity.

00:15:17.910 --> 00:15:20.990
Well... I'm not sure how.

00:15:22.480 --> 00:15:25.300
It has cells called electrocytes.

00:15:25.940 --> 00:15:27.580
And it has electric organs that

00:15:27.580 --> 00:15:30.110
have a lot of those electrocytes 
within them, throughout its body.

00:15:30.830 --> 00:15:35.220
It uses them to magnify the electricity 
that flows through its nerves.

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:37.620
Huh...

00:15:39.110 --> 00:15:40.370
Was that a bit too complicated?

00:15:44.720 --> 00:15:47.740
But that's awesome.

00:15:51.510 --> 00:15:55.170
Hey, it lit up! It lit up! That's so cool!

00:16:05.170 --> 00:16:06.980
Happy birthday.

00:16:10.490 --> 00:16:12.800
Well, this isn't good.

00:16:13.490 --> 00:16:15.350
It does look good on you, after all.

00:16:15.350 --> 00:16:16.830
What am I going to do

00:16:16.830 --> 00:16:20.500
if the other girls catch on 
to your hidden handsomeness?

00:16:21.010 --> 00:16:22.510
You won't have to worry about that.

00:16:23.420 --> 00:16:24.340
Thanks.

00:16:26.080 --> 00:16:29.440
By the way, I have another present for you.

00:16:29.440 --> 00:16:31.710
What? You shouldn't have...

00:16:31.710 --> 00:16:33.100
Oh, come on.

00:16:33.500 --> 00:16:35.140
Make sure you keep facing forward.

00:16:35.140 --> 00:16:36.760
Wait, what are you...?

00:16:49.700 --> 00:16:50.830
You know...

00:16:51.650 --> 00:16:53.520
Out of all of the days I've been alive,

00:16:54.910 --> 00:16:56.890
today is the happiest.

00:17:00.450 --> 00:17:04.780
<i>I remember my mother telling 
me when I was really young,</i>

00:17:05.550 --> 00:17:09.950
<i>that I needed to find someone I love 
just like she found my father.</i>

00:17:10.370 --> 00:17:12.350
<i>And be happy...</i>

00:17:19.950 --> 00:17:23.760
<i>As my mother said, I found happiness.</i>

00:17:25.400 --> 00:17:26.760
<i>That's what I thought.</i>

00:17:39.260 --> 00:17:44.000
<i>Why am I remembering 
that at a time like this?</i>

00:17:46.240 --> 00:17:48.250
<i>That ended long ago.</i>

00:17:48.760 --> 00:17:53.280
<i>It came to light a year ago, 
and ended a year ago.</i>

00:18:24.660 --> 00:18:25.830
I'm sorry.

00:18:27.640 --> 00:18:31.580
I knew that it would hurt you...

00:18:33.060 --> 00:18:34.760
That I needed to stop...

00:18:35.550 --> 00:18:37.270
I needed to stop...

00:18:37.820 --> 00:18:38.890
And yet...

00:18:42.580 --> 00:18:45.350
Because I'm weak...

00:18:46.550 --> 00:18:50.580
I was lonely... and I couldn't help it...

00:18:51.330 --> 00:18:53.940
I'm sorry. I'm awful.

00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:58.500
I can't believe this myself.

00:18:59.970 --> 00:19:03.540
No matter what I say, 
it'll sound like an excuse...

00:19:03.540 --> 00:19:04.880
But...

00:19:05.900 --> 00:19:07.450
Please forgive me.

00:19:08.840 --> 00:19:12.300
I'll never do something like this again.

00:19:13.080 --> 00:19:17.730
I love you. I swear to God, 
that much is true.

00:19:18.930 --> 00:19:21.590
Please believe me.

00:19:35.430 --> 00:19:36.780
I love you, too.

00:19:41.150 --> 00:19:42.520
Ado-kun.

00:19:43.820 --> 00:19:45.160
Thank you.

00:19:46.610 --> 00:19:47.960
Thank you.

00:19:49.810 --> 00:19:52.880
Thank you. Thank you.

00:19:58.470 --> 00:20:02.370
Hey, no crying. I'll feed you in a sec.

00:20:17.550 --> 00:20:21.450
We checked to see if the child 
inherited your Mosaic Organ.

00:20:22.580 --> 00:20:26.000
From the results, it appears that it did not.

00:20:26.500 --> 00:20:31.410
Unless it's acquired later in life, 
it's not something that's usually inherited.

00:20:31.410 --> 00:20:36.920
Indeed. However, the problem is... 
it inherited nothing from you.

00:20:41.480 --> 00:20:43.730
Not even your genes.

00:20:44.880 --> 00:20:48.530
This isn't something 
I'd usually bring up with you.

00:20:50.310 --> 00:20:52.320
However, you'll be departing for Mars soon.

00:20:52.900 --> 00:20:54.900
Make sure you settle things by then.

00:21:00.760 --> 00:21:03.900
<i>I didn't know what to do anymore.</i>

00:21:04.710 --> 00:21:08.660
<i>I couldn't even go back to being an 
eel attached to an electrode anymore.</i>

00:21:15.320 --> 00:21:17.290
Hello, it's me.

00:21:17.830 --> 00:21:19.240
I'm coming home now.

00:21:21.140 --> 00:21:23.610
Yeah, I love you, too.

00:21:30.920 --> 00:21:31.560
<i>Kill...</i>

00:21:32.430 --> 00:21:33.560
<i>Kill me...</i>

00:21:52.480 --> 00:21:53.410
<i>Come.</i>

00:22:01.870 --> 00:22:03.050
<i>I'll kill you.</i>

00:23:35.060 --> 00:23:40.530
<b><i>A Single Drop From 
a Thunderstorm</i></b>
